# Raw SEBI source documents are not committed by default.
corpus/
*.pdf

# ...with one exception. The worked example has to reach the repository, or a
# clone and a deployment both boot to an empty screen and a reviewer concludes
# the product does nothing. It is SEBI's own published circular, freely
# downloadable, 4.8 MB.
#
# The negation needs both lines: git will not look inside an ignored directory,
# so the directory has to be un-ignored before a file within it can be.
!corpus/
corpus/*
!corpus/stock-brokers-master-circular-2025-06-17.pdf

# And the two Investment Adviser editions, for the same reason.
#
# SEBI issued that circular in June 2025 and reissued it in February 2026,
# renumbering 376 clauses. Comparing the two is the amendment demonstration,
# and the Docker build registers both as workspaces so the comparison screen
# opens ready. Leaving them untracked meant a fresh clone built an image with
# no second edition, so the deployed site said "there is nothing to compare
# this against yet" and the strongest thing the product does could not be
# shown. 2.3 MB for the two.
!corpus/investment-advisers-2025-06-27.pdf
!corpus/investment-advisers-2026-02.pdf

# Local databases and parse artifacts
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
out/

# The compiled store. Same reasoning: rules.json carries the 1,377 compiled
# obligations and the 183 signatures the whole demo is a view of.
#
# users.json and workspaces/ are deliberately still ignored. Those are one
# person's account and one person's uploaded documents, and neither belongs in
# a public repository or in a shared deployment.
.sanhita/*
!.sanhita/rules.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Fonts. Committed so the deployed page does not fall back to a system face;
# Inter is SIL Open Font License, which permits redistribution.
!ui/fonts/


# ── Working material, not the product ────────────────────────────────
#
# All of this is real and useful and none of it belongs in a public
# repository. It stays on this machine; it does not reach GitHub.

# The assistant's standing instructions for this repository.
CLAUDE.md

# Internal notes: which deck figures were wrong and what replaced them, the
# competition brief, prior art, open decisions, the claims register. The
# claims register in particular lists claims marked FALSE that must not be
# repeated, which is exactly the kind of working note that reads very badly
# out of context.
DECK-CORRECTIONS.md
GOLD-SET-REVIEW.md
data/

# The raw Inter download, 60 MB. The app loads `ui/fonts/*.woff2`, which is
# 1.1 MB and committed; this is the unpacked source archive it came from and
# nothing references it. `.dockerignore` already keeps it out of the image.
themes/

# Evaluation output. Regenerated by `sanhita eval` and `sanhita export`, so a
# committed copy is a stale copy waiting to contradict a live run.
eval/

# GOLD-SET-RULINGS.yaml is deliberately NOT here. `sanhita eval` reads it to
# decide whether per-field accuracy may be published, and two tests read it,
# so a clone without it cannot run its own evaluation. It carries seven
# rulings and a name, nothing private.
